<title>USA: Dean Witter cuts cash in asset allocation.</title>
<headline>Dean Witter cuts cash in asset allocation.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dean Witter has cut the cash allocation in its basic asset portfolio by five percent and invested it in stocks, chief investment strategist Peter Canelo said on Monday.</p>
<p>He said the company cut its cash allocation to 20 percent from 25, and raised its stock allocation to 60 percent from 55.</p>
<p>Bonds were left unchanged at 20 percent.</p>
<p>-- Wall Street Desk (212) 869-1730</p>
</text>
